uhCkk4JktS3ZkemriQcwSRgEyCDcE5Uv0PCx9yaR.description:
{
  "outcome": "A model running entirely on the local machine — no calls leaving the host — drives the full clarity-tree loop: the in-app chat hands it the tree, it calls read_tree, proposes a well-formed propose_edits ProjectDiff, and the human Confirms it. This is the headline 'fully locally running LLM' example: Acorn's agentic tree-editing works air-gapped. Stack: LFM2.5-8B-A1B (Ollama) driven through the OpenCode ACP agent, all on a no-GPU laptop.",
  "spec": "MODEL: LiquidAI LFM2.5-8B-A1B (GGUF, Q4_K_M ~5.16GB) — a 'lfm2moe' MoE with ~1B ACTIVE params per token, CPU/edge-friendly; Liquid positions it for agentic tool-use. It emits PYTHONIC tool calls between <|tool_call_start|> tokens (its OWN format, not Anthropic Messages), so the claude-agent-acp path (harness:openrouter) is a poor fit; run it under Ollama, whose template parses those tokens into standard tool_calls.\n\nACP AGENT — DECIDED 2026-06-18 (research): OpenCode, launched as a stdio ACP agent with `opencode acp`. Chosen because OpenCode's ACPSessionManager accepts mcpServers passed per-session via ACP session/new — exactly how Acorn's sidecar attaches read_tree/propose_edits (sidecar.js newSession mcpServers) — and it exposes 75+ providers incl. Ollama.\n\nBUILT 2026-06-18: `yarn harness:local` (root package.json) sets OPENCODE_CONFIG=web/dev-harness/opencode.local.json + ACORN_HARNESS_CMD='opencode acp'. opencode.local.json declares provider=ollama (baseURL http://localhost:11434/v1) + model lfm2.5:8b-a1b. dev-harness/README.md documents the stack, the OLLAMA_CONTEXT_LENGTH bump, the tiny-project rule, the egress-block check, and the Goose fallback. STILL TO RUN LIVE: pull the model, raise context, and drive the loop on a tiny project.\n\nGoose is the fallback ACP agent (MCP-native, ACP server, Ollama via OLLAMA_HOST=http://localhost:11434).\n\nTHREE THINGS TO VERIFY LIVE:\n1. TOOL ATTACHMENT (residual risk): confirm the Acorn MCP tools actually attach via ACP session/new in opencode — there is a reported class of 'session/new MCP servers don't work in ACP mode' bug. Fallback if they don't: register acornToolsServer (already bridges to the sidecar via ACORN_WEB_PORT) directly in opencode.local.json under `mcp`.\n2. CONTEXT: read_tree on THIS project is ~137k chars (~40k tokens); Ollama's default context is 4096 — raise OLLAMA_CONTEXT_LENGTH and run the demo against a TINY 3–6 node project.\n3. TOOL TEMPLATE: Ollama issue #15953 reported smaller LFM2.5 builds not accepting tool calls despite supporting them — confirm the 8b-a1b build enables it.\n\nThe binding constraint stays tool-calling fidelity: can LFM2-8B-A1B emit a well-formed propose_edits ProjectDiff for a small tree?",
  "completionCriteria": [
    {
      "statement": "With egress to api.anthropic.com (and other model APIs) blocked, an in-app chat message against a SMALL demo project is answered by LFM2.5-8B-A1B on localhost (Ollama) via the opencode ACP agent, which calls read_tree and emits a propose_edits draft the human Confirms — captured with model + host config as evidence",
      "evaluator": "human"
    },
    {
      "statement": "A single documented dev command (yarn harness:local) brings up the local Ollama-backed opencode ACP backend so the example is reproducible",
      "evaluator": "human",
      "evidence": "2026-06-18 BUILT (awaiting Eric's live run): yarn harness:local added to root package.json; web/dev-harness/opencode.local.json (provider=ollama, model lfm2.5:8b-a1b); dev-harness/README.md 'Fully-local LLM' section with the 3-step runbook. The command + config exist; live execution still pending."
    }
  ],
  "artifacts": [
    {
      "type": "workproduct",
      "label": "package.json — harness:local dev script (OPENCODE_CONFIG + ACORN_HARNESS_CMD='opencode acp')",
      "uri": "package.json"
    },
    {
      "type": "workproduct",
      "label": "opencode.local.json — OpenCode config: provider=ollama (localhost:11434/v1), model lfm2.5:8b-a1b",
      "uri": "web/dev-harness/opencode.local.json"
    },
    {
      "type": "workproduct",
      "label": "dev-harness/README.md — 'Fully-local LLM' section: runbook, OLLAMA_CONTEXT_LENGTH, tiny-project rule, egress check, Goose fallback",
      "uri": "web/dev-harness/README.md"
    },
    {
      "type": "reference",
      "label": "LFM2.5-8B-A1B-GGUF model card (Q4_K_M 5.16GB; lfm2moe ~1B active; edge/on-device)",
      "uri": "https://huggingface.co/LiquidAI/LFM2.5-8B-A1B-GGUF"
    },
    {
      "type": "reference",
      "label": "OpenCode ACP docs — `opencode acp` runs it as a stdio ACP agent",
      "uri": "https://opencode.ai/docs/acp/"
    },
    {
      "type": "reference",
