onversation to tree\\\" button. and I clicked it, and it did not attach it to the open node (I think). I beleive I had opened [[branch-transcript]] but the conversatoin got attached to a child.   But I think that's ok.I guess [[192260]] needs to be completed first?\",\"timestamp\":1782874333271,\"selection\":[{\"actionHash\":\"uhCkk8DruHy_HLNxTLRYsgXqiLr_-sB79TiteYkh_O63_piCwXbgn\",\"id\":\"192260\",\"content\":\"A control attaches the active chat session to the branch it shaped\"}]},{\"role\":\"agent\",\"content\":\"Good news first: the loop **worked end-to-end** — a real transcript got captured, attached, and committed. It's living on `#177483` now (the conversation-artifact leaf), and if you open that node you should see the thread render. So the branch's integration path (attach → commit → renders) is proven. It just landed on the wrong node.\\n\\n**Why it hit a child, not `branch-transcript`:** the target defaults to the **LCA of the nodes this session edited**, and that edited-set is collected live per in-memory session — it **resets on reload/commit**. By the time you clicked Attach, the only edit the panel still had tracked was to `#177483` itself, so `LCA({177483}) = 177483`. Your *selection* (branch-transcript) wasn't consulted because that's only the **no-edits fallback**, and there was an edit. So: correct per the algorithm, surprising in practice.\\n\\nTwo real limits collided:\\n1. **No override picker** — you couldn't say \\\"actually, put it on the node I have open.\\\" That's the one open task on `[[192260]]`, so yes: to make this behave the way you expected, that leaf needs finishing.\\n2. **The edited-set is narrower than the true \\\"branch it shaped\\\"** because it's per-in-memory-session (transcripts don't carry diff args, so I can't reconstruct the full multi-session edit set).\\n\\nMy suggestion — two small changes that together fix what you hit:\\n- **(A) Build the target-override picker** (completes `192260`): the attach control shows the computed target but lets you retarget to any node — defaulting the picker to the **currently-open node** when there is one. That directly gives you \\\"attach to the node I'm looking at.\\\"\\n- **(B) Fold the anchor into the LCA candidate set** — compute `LCA(editedNodes ∪ firstTurnAnchor)` instead of edits-only. Since you had `branch-transcript` open when the conversation began, that pulls the default *up* to `branch-transcript` naturally, which is what you wanted.\\n\\nWant me to build **(A)+(B)**? That closes the last task on `192260` and makes the default land where you'd expect, while still letting you override.\",\"timestamp\":1782874333271},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"yes. Also we probably need to add another leaf here that We don't want to be adding duplicates of the conversation all over the place as it grows, we want to make sure to do appends, or something like that to not be blowing out the DHT with multiple copies.\\n\\n Also I'm noticing that [[192260]] isn't clickable, I thought it was supposed to be.\",\"timestamp\":1782875240245,\"selection\":[{\"actionHash\":\"uhCkk8DruHy_HLNxTLRYsgXqiLr_-sB79TiteYkh_O63_piCwXbgn\",\"id\":\"192260\",\"content\":\"A control attaches the active chat session to the branch it shaped\"}]},{\"role\":\"system\",\"content\":\"↻ sent updated tree\",\"timestamp\":1782875240245},{\"role\":\"agent\",\"content\":\"Compacting...\\n\\nCompacting completed.I'll dig into the clickability question and the current attach wiring before proposing. Let me read the relevant files.Let me check how HarnessChat renders user vs agent messages — that's the likely cause of the clickability gap.Confirmed the bug: user/system chat messages render as raw `{m.text}` (line 980), only agent messages go through `RichText`. So `[[192260]]`/`[[branch-transcript]]` in *your* message are never linkified. `192260` would resolve fine (the regex accepts digits and `resolveRef` handles hashCodeId) — it just never gets the chance.\\n\\nLet me read the attach wiring to plan (A)+(B).Diagnosis complete. Now let me build. I'll track this with tasks.Now the code. First (B) — fold the anchor into the LCA with a root-guard:Now add tests for (B):Now (A) override picker + (D) upsert-by-session. First the imports:Now (3) — render user messages through RichText so `[[192260]]` and `[[branch-transcript]]` are clickable in your own messages too:52/52 (the two new LCA-fold tests included). Now typecheck the touched files:Tests green (52/52, including the two anchor-fold cases) and `tsc` clean on touched files. Now I'll open the review draft — the new dedup leaf + the results for the attach leaf:All built, tests green (52/52), `tsc` clean on touched files, and the review draft is open.\\n\\n## What I built (code)\\n\\n**(B) Anchor folded into the LCA** — `conversationAttach.ts`: `computeAttachTarget` now computes `LCA(edits ∪ first-turn anchor)`, so the target rises to the branch you had open when the conversation began. A **root-guard** keeps an *unrelated* anchor from dragging a well-scoped edit set up to the root. +2 tests (an ancestor anchor raises the target; an unrelated one doesn't) → **14 tests**.\\n\\n**(A) Target-override picker** — `attachConversation` (HarnessChat) now shows the computed target with *why* it was chosen, and lets you **accept it or type any node** (handle / 6-digit id / actionHash, resolved via `resolveRef`) before the draft opens. That's the last open task on the attach leaf, now closed.\\n\\n**Dedup / no-duplicate-copies (the new concern)** — attach now **upserts by `sessionId`**: re-attaching the same session to a node replaces its existing conversation artifact in place instead of appending another copy.\\n\\n**Clickability fix** — the real cause: user/system chat messages rendered as raw `{m.text}`; only *agent* messages went through `RichText`. So `[[192260]]`/`[[branch-transcript]]` in **your own message** were never linkified (the regex + `resolveRef` handle numeric hashCodeIds fine — they just never got rendered). Now **user messages render through `RichText`**, so handles you type are clickable too. System notices (\\\"↻ sent updated tree\\\") stay plain.\\n\\n## In the draft (open for your Confirm)\\n- **New leaf** under `branch-transcript`: *\\\"One canonical conversation artifact per session — re-attach updates in place, never duplicates.\\\"* Task 1 (upsert-by-sessionId) marked done; the [[handle]]-reference-not-copy, grow-in-place, and multi-node guard tasks left open.\\n- **Attach leaf (`192260`)**: all 6 tasks now checked (override picker done), spec updated for (A)+(B), executable criterion evidence refreshed (14 tests). Its human criterion stays unconfirmed → it'll read as **awaiting your evaluation**.\\n\\nTwo notes:\\n1. The clickability fix technically extends the **handle-link** leaf (it's already Achieved). I left that node untouched to avoid churning a large Achieved node — say the word and I'll record the fix there.\\n2. Once you Confirm, `[[192260]]` in this very message should become clickable, and re-clicking **Attach** with `branch-transcript` open should now target it (anchor-fold) — or use the new prompt to retarget explicitly.\",\"timestamp\":1782875240245,\"toolCalls\":[{\"id\":\"toolu_01EFr8z3UXEtz5rNLTZpkP1k\",\"title\":\"\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"id\":\"toolu_01DUtUWHWy4s2EABWtp2jhSa\",\"title\":\"\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"id\":\"toolu_01P5vQ6PK4QjHZjP7XFfs2wR\",\"title\":\"\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"id\":\"toolu_01Usmr2x8qgi8wYYCZMusHtx\",\"title\":\"\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"id\":\"toolu_014X39ReAuE5BxaQMqtTVFUc\",\"title\":\"\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"id\":\"toolu_01XMwG6znHXLgVMiK1FwxtrV\",\"title\":\"\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"id\":\"toolu_01RTZwuCffmhJaTaoJAyNybR\",\"title\":\"\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"id\":\"toolu_013WwjkVvfVn8pCTKvfKYLpi\",\"title\":\"\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"id\":\"toolu_014TfFRXS7ZBLGyrvSMEB7X4\",\"title\":\"\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"id\":\"toolu_0