uhCkk8DruHy_HLNxTLRYsgXqiLr_-sB79TiteYkh.description:
{
  "outcome": "From the in-app chat panel a human attaches the active session's captured transcript to the branch it shaped, creating a single conversation artifact on it. The target is not guessed: it defaults to the lowest common ancestor of the nodes the session actually edited, and when the session made no edits it falls back to the conversation's ANCHORED selection — the node that was selected when the opening question was asked, not whatever the human has since navigated to. Because all writes go through review, the attachment arrives as a propose_edits draft the human confirms.",
  "spec": "An 'attach this conversation' control in HarnessChat computes a default target node:\n1. Take the lowest common ancestor of the nodes the session created/edited — 'the branch it shaped'. The conversation's ask-time anchor (first user turn's selection) is FOLDED INTO the LCA set so the target rises to the branch that was open when the conversation began; a root-guard keeps an unrelated anchor from dragging a well-scoped edit set up to the root.\n2. If the session made no edits (pure discussion), fall back to the ANCHORED selection = the FIRST user turn's send-time selection. NEVER the live current selection.\n3. If the LCA degenerates to the root (unrelated branches), ask rather than dumping at the top.\nThe human then ACCEPTS the computed target or OVERRIDES it to any node (handle / 6-digit id / actionHash, resolved via resolveRef) before the propose_edits draft is submitted.\n\nIMPLEMENTED 2026-06-30: web/src/harness/conversationAttach.ts (pure) — lowestCommonAncestor + computeAttachTarget now fold the anchor into the LCA set with a root-guard. HarnessChat.attachConversation: collects edited node ids (editedNodesRef), builds the transcript, computes the target, shows a target-override prompt (accept or type any node ref), UPSERTS the conversation artifact by sessionId on the chosen node (no duplicate copies), and submits via the same propose_edits draft path the agent uses.\n\nNOTE — edited-node source: the transcript's tool calls hold {id,title,status} but NOT their diff args, so edited node ids come from HarnessChat's live per-session collection of propose_edits targets (editedNodesRef), which RESETS on reload — so across sessions the LCA can be narrower than the whole multi-session effort; the override picker is the escape hatch. Unresolvable draft ids are filtered by computeAttachTarget.\n\nRelies-on propose_edits, the capture leaf (first-turn ask-time selection), the conversation artifact type, and node-ref-resolver (resolveRef).",
  "completionCriteria": [
    {
      "statement": "Attaching proposes the LCA of edited nodes (with the ask-time anchor folded in) as the default target; for a no-edits session it proposes the FIRST user turn's ask-time selection (never the live selection, never the latest turn's); the human can override to any node; confirming adds/updates one conversation artifact on the chosen node and it renders there",
      "evaluator": "human",
      "evidence": "2026-06-30 BUILT, awaiting Eric live verify: the 'Attach conversation to tree' button computes the target (LCA of this session's edits with the first-turn anchor folded in; else the anchor; root-LCA asks), then a prompt lets you ACCEPT it or type any node (handle / 6-digit id / actionHash) to retarget. It upserts by sessionId (re-attaching the same session updates in place, no duplicate) and opens a propose_edits DRAFT adding/updating the conversation artifact on the chosen node. To verify: chat + have the agent propose an edit, click Attach, accept or retarget, Confirm, open the node — the thread renders.",
